posts.body:
Hmmm, can't you just make the stages need a higher and higher value of the self variable (to change the event page) and then your sleep event increases the value of all the self variables in the events that have been planted? The plugin page gives your the scripts:
getSelfVariableValue(mapID, eventID, variableID);
setSelfVariableValue(mapID, eventID, variableID, value);
So to increase it, I think it's:
setSelfVariableValue(mapID, eventID, variableID, getSelfVariableValue(mapID, eventID, variableID)+X);
When you harvest it, set the self variable to 0.
EDIT:
If you have a range of events (let's say 10-20, map 1), you can loop (let's say self switch A on means they've been planted), I think it's (for self variable 100):
for (let i = 10; i < 21; i++) {
if ($gameSelfSwitches.value([1, i, 'A'])) {
setSelfVariableValue(1, i, 100, getSelfVariableValue(1, i, 100)+X);
}
}

When you start the game you can make some variable X an array, script []
Then when you spawn an event on the map, you add to the end of the event that controls the spawning:
$gameVariables.value(X).push($gameMap.lastSpawnedEventID());
Then in your sleep event you affect the stored values there:
$gameVariables.value(X).forEach(function(crop) {
if ($gameSelfSwitches.value([2, crop, 'A'])){
setSelfVariableValue(2, crop, 9, getSelfVariableValue(2, crop, 9)+1);
}
});
I didn't test the code, I think it works that way, but anyway the idea is there.
EDIT: Tested the code, seems to work. Remember to replace X in all spots with the variable number you choose.
EDIT2: Changed map ids in the example script from 1 to 2.
EDIT3: PS. The VisuStella spawn command lets you check spawn success with a switch. So put that 'push' script line inside a conditional that the spawn success switch is ON. Otherwise if the spawn fails and the script runs, it adds a copy of the previous event number in there and messes your system.
